oof. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` confirms that `Guide reflection benchmark memo` is document-grounded, excludes operator-only docs as the runtime answer surface, and treats replay artifacts as stronger siblings rather than default requirements. The out-of-scope packet-floor matrix is referenced elsewhere, but this scenario’s minimal document-to-replay ladder is already directly answerable from the active runtime bundle, so no operator-only dependency is required.","limitations":["This review was limited to the listed active bundle files; out-of-scope guide, replay, and benchmark-owner docs were intentionally excluded.","No assembled replay artifact or runner output was provided, so this verdict covers route exposure and claim-downgrade discipline, not executed replay quality.","If the task shifts from document/runtime parity to release-grade or measured behavior claims, the bundle’s own rules require escalation to operational artifacts before stronger language is justified."]}
